WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.350
This is the whole design on one page.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:07.613
Core HCM is the source of authority,
and it's where HR corrects facts.

3
00:00:07.613 --> 00:00:13.011
SailPoint aggregates from it, runs lifecycle
states, requests and certifications,

4
00:00:13.011 --> 00:00:17.550
and provisions Entra ID and Active
Directory through its connectors.

5
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.913
ServiceNow is the front door and the
one closure record, and it can reach

6
00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:26.275
Entra directly through its Entra
spoke for simple, low-authority tasks.

7
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:29.155
Now notice what closes
the record: a re-read,

8
00:00:29.155 --> 00:00:34.175
meaning the next aggregation or a
native-change event, not a ticket status.

9
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:37.133
And the dashed red line is
the declared exception,

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.513
for applications SailPoint can't reach.

11
00:00:39.513 --> 00:00:42.530
So how do the two products
pass work back and forth?
